explanation:
Terrace farming is typically practiced in mountainous regions where there are few natural stretches of flat land needed to plant crops. There was little need for such a labor-intensive technique in the U.S. Southwest or the Mississippi River Valley, and other methods of intensive agriculture (the island 
chinampas
) were developed for the jungle conditions of Mesoamerica. It was the people of the Andes, most notably the Inca, who became terrace farmers.
